  "methodology": "Each EFCA district territory was approximated as a set of US counties (whole-state for districts with no boundary overlap, specific county lists for the 13 states split between multiple districts \u2014 see us_view_district_crosswalk.json for those lists). For each district, avg_risk and each hazard score is the SIMPLE (unweighted) average of that field across every county assigned to the district; sum_pop is the straight sum of 2020 Census population across those counties. Hazard scores (0-100) are FEMA's normalized, nationally-percentiled Risk Index score for that hazard type \u2014 not a probability, a relative-severity ranking versus every other US county.",
  "hazard_codes": {
    "AVLN": "Avalanche",
    "CFLD": "Coastal Flooding",
    "CWAV": "Cold Wave",
