  "caveats": [
    "This is a best-effort APPROXIMATION built from real church-location evidence, not an official EFCA boundary file \u2014 see us_view_district_crosswalk.json and district_boundary_crosswalk.md for per-state confidence levels and known ambiguities (e.g. a contested church in Louisville, KY; a contested town in Minnesota).",
    "A hazard score of 0 means FEMA NRI had no non-null value for that hazard across every county in the district (i.e. the hazard is not applicable there, e.g. Avalanche in the Deep South) \u2014 it is not a computed zero-risk finding.",
    "Total counties across all 17 districts (3,122) is slightly below the ~3,144 US total; the shortfall is real, documented gap counties in split states where no church evidence existed for any neighboring district (see district_boundary_crosswalk.md, e.g. central South Dakota, mid-Michigan Upper Peninsula) \u2014 not a processing error."
